5. DEFAULT DELIVERY POLICY

Implement the following configurable business rules:

STANDARD DELIVERY

Default maximum road distance: 10 km.

Restaurant must be approved, active, accepting orders, and within its configured service area.

Restaurant must have an eligible delivery method and sufficient delivery capacity.

Menu items must be active, in stock, and orderable.

The routing engine must return a valid route.

The final road distance must not exceed the effective delivery limit.

EXTENDED DELIVERY

Default disabled.

Configurable per restaurant and by authorized administrators.

Suggested initial extended limit: 20 km.

Requires explicit approval, compatible delivery arrangements, and valid pricing.

Must not be activated merely because the customer PIN code matches.

LONG-DISTANCE DELIVERY

Disabled by default.

Suggested maximum policy limit: 100 km, only if an appropriate logistics service is implemented and approved.

Treat this as a separate delivery/logistics mode, not normal restaurant delivery.

Require supported routes, packaging and food-safety procedures, capacity, serviceable destination, realistic ETA, and explicit pricing.

Do not display long-distance delivery as available until the complete logistics workflow is operational.

Allow platform administrators to configure these settings safely.

Keep separate fields for:

Platform default radius.

Restaurant-specific approved maximum radius.

Customer-selected delivery address.

Effective delivery limit.

Service mode.

Actual road distance.

Route duration.

Delivery eligibility result.

Do not allow a restaurant to exceed its administrator-approved maximum radius.

