For multiple restaurants, use a supported routing table/matrix endpoint where appropriate. Validate the response and map each result back to the correct restaurant ID.

Calculate the estimated total delivery time using configurable components:

Estimated delivery time =
restaurant preparation time

estimated route travel time

dispatch/assignment buffer

pickup and handoff buffer.

Avoid adding the same time component twice.

OSRM's ordinary route duration must not be presented as guaranteed live-traffic ETA. Label estimates appropriately and use traffic-aware data only if the selected provider actually supports it.

If routing fails:

Apply bounded retries where appropriate.

Record a structured error.

Do not fabricate road distance or ETA.

Do not confirm a new delivery order without the required eligibility verification.

Show a friendly temporary-unavailability message.

